ther login, another tab, another interruption.\n\nThe daily summary closes that gap. Every morning, a clear snapshot of your open tickets arrives where your team already works, so everyone starts the day on the same page.\n\n## What's in each summary\n\nPosted at the time you choose, each digest includes:\n\n- **Total open tickets**, broken down by priority\n- **Unassigned tickets** that still need an owner\n- **Tickets awaiting a response**, so nothing goes stale\n- **Your oldest open ticket**, because aging issues shouldn't hide\n- **A direct link** to jump straight into the full queue\n\nOne message. Ten seconds to read. A complete picture of the day ahead.\n\n## Set up in under two minutes\n\n1. Go to **Settings → Integrations → Slack**\n2. Click **Connect to Slack** and authorize your workspace\n3. Pick your channel and delivery time\n4. Save — your first summary arrives tomorrow morning\n\nNo admin approval workflows, no configuration files, no downtime.\n\n## A few ways teams are using it\n\n- **Support leads** post summaries to their team channel each morning to kick off triage\n- **Engineering teams** follow the support channel to spot bug reports trending upward\n- **Executives** get visibility into support health without asking for a report\n\n## Available today\n\nThe Slack integration is live now for all customers, on every plan, at no additional cost.\n\n**Ready to try it?**\n\n[Connect Slack now →] | [Read the setup guide →]\n\nAs always, we'd love your feedback — tell us what you'd like to see in future summaries at [support email].\n\nHere's to fewer surprises hiding in the queue.\n\n— The [Product Name] Team\n\n---\n\n*Word count: ~360. Placeholders in brackets — product name, links, and contact email — can be swapped in before publishing. Happy to adjust the tone (more formal, more playful), trim it for email format, or add a FAQ section if helpful.*\n=== END OF TEXT A ===\n\n=== TEXT B ===\n**New Feature: Daily Ticket Summaries for Slack**\n\nHi there,\n\nStarting your day buried in the support queue? Not anymore.\n\nWe're excited to launch **Daily Digest for Slack** — a simple new integration that posts a clear, skimmable summary of your open support tickets to a Slack channel of your choice, every morning.\n\nBuilt for busy support teams, it's the easiest way to keep everyone aligned without living in the helpdesk.\n\n**What you get**\n\nEvery weekday morning at the time you choose, you'll get an automated post with:\n\n* Total open tickets, broken down by status and priority\n* New tickets since yesterday\n* Tickets at risk of breaching SLA\n* Your 5 oldest unresolved tickets, with direct links\n\nNo digging. No manual reports. Just the context you need to prioritize, right where your team already works.\n\n**Why you'll love it**\n\nCustomers in our beta told us it changed their standups. Support leads spot bottlenecks faster, agents know what to tackle first, and stakeholders outside support — like product and success — finally have visibility without needing another login.\n\n**How to turn it on**\n\nIt takes less than 2 minutes:\n\n1. Go to **Settings > Integrations > Slack** and click Connect\n2. Choose the channel where you want the digest (we recommend #support-daily)\n3. Pick your delivery time and timezone\n\nThat's it. Your first digest will arrive tomorrow morning.\n\nDaily Digest for Slack is available now on all plans at no extra cost.\n\nTry it this week and let us know what you think — just reply to this email or reach out via chat. We built this for you, and your feedback shapes what's next.\n\nThanks for being a customer,\n\nThe Team\n=== END OF TEXT B ===\n\nAnswer with a single JSON object and nothing else:\n{\"more_ai\": \"A\" or \"B\", \"confidence\": 1-5, \"tells_A\": [\"short tell\", ...], \"tells_B\": [\"short tell\", ...]}\n"
